 to the boliw, the traditional and mystical sources of their power, or attend to the ancestral shrines that had long sustained this warrior state, they came to regard Islam as an increasingly precious resource, a set of beliefs and practices capable of not only protecting themselves but of assuring the continued vitality of all of Segou and its citizenry." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 896, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 792})
