um. The Somali tribes merged Islam, headed by the wadād (the religious priest and spiritual leader) into their lives. Local beliefs survived among the Somali tribes alongside the Sharī‘a and the Quran. Even after fully adopting Islam, especially during the times of Gragn, the Somalis continued to adhere to a variety of popular beliefs, witchcraft, and sorcery." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 906, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 744})
