een gods or spirits, on the one hand, and their client communities, families, and individuals, on the other. They did so in both directions, channeling requests and messages between humans and gods. [...] Finally, transcendence seekers, Daoist adepts, and Buddhist monks also numbered among the specialists called upon by laypersons for assistance, healing, and protection—including protection against the demands of local gods, the depredations of ghosts and demons, and even in some cases the power of spirit mediums." '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 920, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 782})
